#: lumos.core.priors:1 of
msgid "Prior distributions attached to free parameters (REQ-EL-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors:3 of
msgid ""
"Priors describe what is known about a free parameter before calibration or inference. They carry physical "
"units, so they can be checked against the parameter they are attached to. Plain numbers are accepted for "
"dimensionless parameters. Sampling and log-densities are added with the inference blocks (phase 17)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.LogUniform:1 of
msgid "Log-uniform distribution between ``low`` and ``high`` (``0 < low < high``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.LogUniform:3 of
msgid "Suited to scale parameters known only to an order of magnitude (fluxes, contrasts...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.Normal:1 of
msgid "Normal (Gaussian) distribution of mean ``mean`` and standard deviation ``std > 0``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.Prior:1 of
msgid "Base class of prior distributions."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.Prior:3 of
msgid "Subclasses are frozen dataclasses whose first field fixes the unit of the distribution."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.Prior.unit:1 of
msgid "Unit of the values described by the prior."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.Uniform:1 of
msgid "Uniform distribution between ``low`` and ``high`` (``low < high``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.priors.prior_from_json:1 of
