msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.signal:1 of
msgid "Abstract signal types flowing between elements (``REQ-SIG-*``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.signal:3 of
msgid ""
"The hierarchy of signal classes defines which ports can be connected: an output producing a signal of type "
"``T`` can feed an input expecting ``S`` when ``T`` is ``S`` or a subclass of ``S``. Concrete signals "
"(``Wavefront``, ``Wavecube``, ``DataProduct``...) derive from these classes; they arrive in phase 3."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.signal.DataSignal:1 of
msgid "Detected or processed data: images, cubes, time series, scalars..."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.signal.OpticalSignal:1 of
msgid "Light: coherent fields, incoherent bundles, radiance fields, modal amplitudes..."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.signal.Signal:1 of
msgid "Anything that flows along a connection. An input of type ``Signal`` accepts every signal."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port:1 of
msgid "Typed input and output ports of elements (REQ-SIG-11)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port:3 of
msgid "Ports are declared as class attributes::"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port:10 of
