"Reading a port on an instance returns a :class:`PortRef`, which identifies \"this port of this object\" and"
" is what connections are made of (``ctx.connect(source.out, splitter.in_)``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Input:1 of
msgid "An input port."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Input:3 of
msgid "Accepted signal type (subtypes are accepted too)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Input:4 of
msgid "Port name; defaults to the attribute name without its trailing underscore."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Input:5 of
msgid "Whether several connections may feed this input (fan-in). By default an input takes one connection."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Input:7 of
msgid "Description of the port."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.port.Output:1 of
msgid "An output port. An output can feed any number of inputs (fan-out)."
