msgid "Return the ``.lumos`` document describing this element (see :mod:`lumos.io`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Element.from_lumos:1 of
msgid "Create an element from a ``.lumos`` document, checking that it is an instance of ``cls``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Element.describe:1 of
msgid "Return a readable description of the element: fields, values and ports."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Element.schema:1 of
msgid "Return the JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) of the serialised form of this element."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Element.schema:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The serialised body is ``{\"name\": ..., \"params\": {...}, \"settings\": {...}, \"state\": {...}}``, where"
" physical values are encoded with :func:`lumos.units.quantity_to_json`. Information that JSON Schema cannot"
" express (units, bounds, dimension...) is given in ``x-lumos-*`` keywords; unit compatibility and bounds "
"are checked when the element is loaded."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Values:1 of
msgid "Immutable snapshot of the SI values of an element's fields."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.element.Values:3 of
msgid ""
"Values are reachable by key (``values[\"focal_length\"]``) or attribute (``values.focal_length``). Physical"
" fields are floats, complex numbers or read-only arrays in unscaled SI units; settings are returned as they"
" are."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry:1 of
msgid "Registry of element types (specs §10, NF-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry:3 of
msgid ""
"Every element class that can be saved to or loaded from a ``.lumos`` file is registered under a **stable "
"identifier** and a **type version**::"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry:9 of
msgid ""
"Loading a file only instantiates registered classes: the identifier is looked up in the registry, never "
"imported. Identifiers starting with ``lumos.`` are reserved for classes defined in the ``lumos`` package; "
"third-party packages use their own prefix and declare a module to import in the ``lumos.elements`` entry-"
"point group, loaded by :meth:`Registry.load_plugins`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry:14 of
msgid ""
"The type version is incremented when the serialised form of an element changes; migrations from older "
"versions are registered with the ``.lumos`` file format (step P1.6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry:1 of
msgid "Mapping between stable type identifiers and element classes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.register:1 of
msgid "Return a class decorator registering an element class under ``type_id``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.register:3 of
msgid ""
"Dotted identifier: lowercase package segments followed by a class name, for example "
"``\"mylab.optics.ThinLens\"``. The ``lumos.`` prefix is reserved for classes of LUMOS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.register:5 of
msgid "Version of the serialised form (an integer >= 1)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.get:1 of
msgid "Return the class registered under ``type_id``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.version:1 of
msgid "Return the current type version of ``type_id``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.type_id:1 of
msgid "Return the identifier under which ``cls`` is registered."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.add_migration:1 of
msgid "Return a decorator registering the migration of ``type_id`` from ``from_version`` to the next one."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.add_migration:3 of
msgid ""
"A migration receives the serialised body of an element (``name``, ``params``, ``settings``, ``state``) "
"written with type version ``from_version`` and returns the body for version ``from_version + 1``. Loading "
"an old document applies the migrations one version at a time."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.migrate:1 of
msgid "Upgrade ``body`` from ``from_version`` to the current version of ``type_id``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.load_plugins:1 of
msgid "Load the plugins declared in the entry-point ``group`` and return the names of those loaded."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.registry.Registry.load_plugins:3 of
msgid ""
"A plugin entry point designates a module (or object) whose import registers element types. A plugin that "
"fails to load is logged as a warning and skipped, so that one broken plugin does not prevent LUMOS from "
"working."
msgstr ""

